course: dictionary
lesson: 122
title: Adroit: skilful with hands and wits
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Adroit means very skilful. A juggler who keeps five balls in the air is adroit with her hands. «The clever fox made an adroit escape from the farmer's hens.» The fox was quick and smart, so adroit here means quick and clever.
explain: Adroit can also mean good at dealing with people or tricky situations. A smooth talker who gets out of trouble with his words is adroit. Look at the clues: is the person skilful with their hands, or quick and clever with people? Both meanings can fit, so read on to see which one the text means.
explain: Adroit often appears in phrases such as «adroit at», «an adroit move» and «adroit handling». Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. If skilful still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: Adroit means very skilful or clever.
fact: Adroit can describe skilful hands, like a juggler, or a quick, clever way of dealing with people.
fact: Adroit is an adjective, and its forms are adroit, more adroit and most adroit.
fact: «English borrowed gauche to mean clumsy and adroit (from à droit) to mean skilful.» So adroit came into English from French.
fact: The sentence shows an opposite pair: gauche means clumsy, and adroit means skilful, so they are almost opposites.
exercise: «The juggler was adroit, keeping five balls in the air at once.» What does adroit mean here? | Sleepy and slow | Very loud | *Very skilful with the hands
exercise: «The smooth talker gave an adroit reply that got him out of trouble.» What does adroit suggest? | *Quick and clever with people | Wet and grey | Tired | Loud and angry | Clumsy and rude
exercise: Find and copy one word from «The thief made an adroit move and was gone before anyone saw.» that describes a skilful move. | saw | *adroit | thief | before
test: Which sentence uses adroit correctly? | The puppy tripped over its own paws, so it was adroit. | The rain was adroit and wet. | *The goalkeeper made an adroit save to stop the ball.
test: Which word from the lesson is the opposite of adroit in meaning? | Barely | Glum | *Clumsy | Ancient
exam: In «She showed adroit handling of the angry customer», what does adroit mean? | Rude and loud | *Quick and skilful with people | Clumsy and slow | Tired and sad
